// examples/headings.typ
//
// Small pattern: heading levels + a label callout.
//
// Useful for the LLM to crib from when generating multi-section
// documents. Kept short on purpose — Examples are snippets the LLM
// reads to learn a single pattern, not full document skeletons (those
// live under templates/).

= Top-level heading (level 1)

This is body text under a level-1 heading.

== Second-level heading

Body text under level 2.

=== Third-level heading

Body text under level 3 — useful for subsections that don't appear
in the auto-generated table of contents.

#emph[Inline emphasis] and #strong[strong text] round out the
common formatting primitives.
